note bottom
  **P2-1** There is **no CI of any kind** — no `.github/`, `.gitlab-ci.yml`, `Jenkinsfile`,
  `.circleci/`, `Makefile`, `pytest.ini`/`pyproject.toml`, pre-commit config or coverage tooling.
  1 141 passing tests run only when a human types `README.md:298-302`. Wire the three existing
  commands first, then add `next lint`, `npx tsc --noEmit` and a coverage floor. Delete rather
  than bless the 5 tests that cannot fail: `test_search_off.py:9-29` (re-implements the gate
  locally, ends `assert True`), `test_search_engine.py:111-116`
  (`assert settings.search_enabled in (True, False)`),
  `test_conversation_integrity.py:553-566` (monkeypatches the checker to itself),
  `test_chart_pipeline.py:197-199` (`assert x is None or True`),
  `test_history_v3.py:162-176` (posts to a route that 404s).
  **P2-2** `orchestrator/requirements.txt:3-28` is 20 unbounded `>=` pins with **no lockfile**;
  `sync-worker/requirements.txt` already caps majors and `frontend/package-lock.json` is fully
  locked — adopt the sync-worker regime, then digest-pin `nvcr.io/nvidia/vllm:26.05-py3`
  (`Dockerfile:14`) so the deployment stops depending on "never `docker compose pull`"
  (`README.md:273-276`). Add `python-multipart`, `pypdfium2`, `pillow`, `trafilatura` to
  `requirements-dev.txt` — without the first, 12 test files fail at collection on a clean host.
  **P2-3** `db.py:84,102,114,123` declare no foreign key, so `delete_conversation`
  (`db.py:334-340`) orphans `uploads`, `url_documents`, `repos`, `repo_chunks`. Conversation ids
  are client-supplied (`history.py:92-97`), so a recreated id inherits
  **the deleted conversation's rows**.
  **P2-4** `syncworker/storage.py:140` creates every warehouse table with no PRIMARY KEY and no
  index, so the upsert `DELETE … WHERE Id IN (…)` (`:156`) is a full table scan on every batch,
  every 30 minutes, for all 48 objects.
  **P2-5** `db.py:195-205` executes 16 DDL statements plus a full-table de-dup `DELETE`
  (`:181-186`) on **every** call — 34 call sites (31 × `closing(connect())` in `db.py`, plus
  `auth.py:48`, `health.py:79`, `main.py:36`); one `POST /chat` pays it at least six times.
  Migrate once in `lifespan` (`main.py:27-38`) and cache. `auth.py:48` `_oldest_user()` also
  leaks the connection it opens.
  **P2-6** `.env.example:7-14` still solicits `AWS_REGION` / `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` /
  `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` / `SF_SECRET_NAME` for a subsystem deleted on 2026-07-28
  (`syncworker/secrets.py:1-6,172`; `tests/test_secrets.py:72` asserts `boto3` is absent).
  18 of the template's 43 variables reach no container at all — there is no `env_file:` in
  `docker-compose.yml`. `.env.bak-205921` sits plaintext in the working tree (gitignored, mode
  600, but still on disk).
  **P2-7** 42 broad `except Exception` handlers swallow errors across `orchestrator/app`;
  `main.py:161` and `:676` use `contextlib.suppress` around a persist, so a lost answer is
  silent. No correlation id propagates browser → orchestrator → engine → model.
end note

