note bottom
  **P3-1** Three of the eight critical flows have no end-to-end coverage at all.
  **RAG retrieval** — `engines/rag.py` (151 LOC) has zero tests; `run_rag_engine` has no caller
  in the suite, so LanceDB search, the Qwen3-Reranker load path and the citation contract
  `README.md:52-53` calls non-negotiable are unexercised.
  **upload → extract → report → PDF** — `POST /uploads` (`uploads.py:66-71`) is referenced by no
  test; `run_report_engine` (`engines/report.py:214`) and `_run_pandoc` (`:102-121`, which shells
  out to `pandoc --pdf-engine=weasyprint`) never execute, so the `.docx`/`.pdf` artefacts the
  README advertises are never produced in CI.
  **NL → SQL → guard → DuckDB as a composition** — every `fake_chat_completion` in the suite
  returns a benign `SELECT`, so nothing proves a model emitting `DROP TABLE opportunities`
  produces an SSE `error` frame rather than a query. Also join the two SSE halves: no test feeds
  real orchestrator bytes into `frontend/lib/sse.ts readChatStream`.
  **P3-2** `docker-compose.yml:25` sets a ≲0.60 GPU-fraction ceiling, but `--profile vision`
  sums 0.35 + 0.11 + 0.14 + 0.04 = **0.64 ≈ 77 GB of 121 GB**, and the orchestrator holds a
  further GPU reservation for the in-process reranker (`:283-289`, `RERANK_ENABLED: "true"`
  `:244`) that sits outside the budget entirely. The compose header comment `:21-24` and
  `README.md:283-288` both repeat the stale 0.53 sum that omits `vllm-vision`.
  **P3-3** `frontend/README.md:11` still documents Recharts (replaced by ECharts), `:58-67`
  documents `/login`, `middleware.ts` and the `ts_session` cookie (all removed on 2026-07-28),
  `:69-72` documents a model picker that now chooses effort, and `:29` gives an
  `ORCHESTRATOR_URL` default that is wrong inside the compose network.
  `README.md:142` says `SEARCH_MAX_RESULTS=10` while `.env.example:55` and
  `docker-compose.yml:256` say 100. `CHANGELOG.md:205-208` and `:406-412` describe superseded
  models and context windows with no "superseded" marker. `.env.example:4` still names a model
  replaced on 2026-07-28.
end note

